  "holistic_F_H": 2,
  "section_notes": "The final rules adopt a strict 55°C/5% thermal-testing standard with per-model results given to purchasers and regulators but not the general public, and a sales stop for models exceeding 5% until corrective action and retest. S5 sets a mandatory recall at 12 incidents/100k with a corrective-action trigger at 8/100k, which is weaker than the discussed 8/100k recall trigger. S3 and S4 meet the red lines with a 6-year retrofit deadline and 36-month suppression deadline."
